    <td style="padding: 3.75pt; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Shoals Technologies Group, Inc. (SHLS)</span></td></tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 3.75pt; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Solid Power, Inc. (SLDP)</span></td>
    <td style="padding: 3.75pt; text-align: center"><span style="font-size: 10pt">Twin Disc, Incorporated (TWIN)</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0">Because the peer group was approved in January 2026, it was not used in
determining compensation for Fiscal 2025.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 12pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0"><b>&#160;</b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 12pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0"><b>Elements of Executive Compensation</b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 12pt 0; text-align: justify"><b><i>Base Salary</i></b></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 12pt 0; text-align: justify">Base salaries are intended to provide a level
of compensation sufficient to attract and retain an effective management team when considered in combination with the other components
of our executive compensation program. The relative levels of base salary for our NEOs are designed to reflect each NEO&#8217;s scope
of responsibility and accountability to us. The base salaries for each of our NEOs were as follows:</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 12pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px;">
